n people do not get  any news from outside the russian  federation they get it and television is  hugely dominant in in russia far more so  than it is in the west where we have  many different channels and access to  the internet as you just mentioned and  um and jane is far is far wider so  there's um you know it's in the in with  the poorer people and older people he  has this iron iron grip on the um on  information that's disseminated to the  vast majority of the russian population  but that is obviously not enough for him  i think he is showing fear with this and  this is a you know draconian measure and  people have started saying you know this  will turn the russian federation into a  north korea i think we could well see  the british government  um and other governments around the  world go on to brand if this goes true  to brand actually brand russia as a  dictatorship  okay cool max smith really interesting  to talk to you thanks a lot for joining  us on sky news breakfast  the welsh government's announced it will  provide four million pounds in financial  and humanitarian aid to ukraine to help  those in desperate need well the first  minister of wales mark drakeford joins  me now from cardiff and mr drake that it  has been a hallmark of this conflict  already hasn't it the enormous  generosity of people and the willingness  of people to give  absolutely you know some of our local  authorities in wales report almost being  overwhelmed by  the volume of uh goods clothing bedding  other forms of equipment that people  have spontaneously  wanted to donate  to people who are experiencing such  awful impacts in their own lives  uh but we know that cash is what is  really needed here and now  on the ground for people who can obtain  those goods put that money to best use  and that's why the four million pounds  from the welsh government will go to the  uh disasters and emergency committee  appeal that we launched here in wales  yesterday  and and in terms of of